{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b7852e33fff1d9d91156b8be8b6fd7e93f856df803ee7ac6699f35431b748a48","digest":{"component_or_area":"overlap judge / prompt caching","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py","judge_one","judge()","CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS","anthropic_cache_instructions","llm/capabilities.py","reviewers/overlap_judge.md","system_prompt","instructions","_digest_block","shared_side"],"problem_keywords":["prompt caching","input token cost","LLM API efficiency","overlap judge","system prompt optimization"],"propositions":["The query ticket digest is re-sent in the user message on every call in a batch, inflating input tokens despite being byte-identical across calls.","Hoisting the invariant query digest into the system prompt (which carries a cache breakpoint) makes it part of the cacheable prefix, allowing cache reuse across the batch.","The measured effective cache floor for claude-sonnet-4-6 is 1024 tokens, not the 4096 hardcoded for Opus; the hoisted prefix reaches only 846 tokens, staying below the threshold.","Precision is preserved (12/12 verdict-parity on ordered pairs), but token cost rises +936 (+5.8%) due to the orientation paragraph reconciling the prompt framing, because no caching occurs."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787480618376232001,"uuid":"bdf5e7c1-933b-44c6-a88a-8eecb68abf08"}